FINAL OWNER DIRECTIVE — COMPLETE IVX IA AS A TRUE 10/10 SENIOR DEVELOPER

Rork, execute this as the final completion task for IVX IA.

Do not return another certification narrative.

Do not return another “very close” report.

Do not mark COMPLETE because a few acceptance tests passed.

The latest evidence shows major progress, including:

- Root cause identified for lost pending actions.
- Stale state overwrite repaired.
- Property query routing improved.
- Multi-turn property workflow mostly working.
- GitHub and Render SHA parity reported.
- Production deployment reported live.
- Several acceptance turns now pass.

However, the screenshots also show that the system required repeated manual fixes, multiple deployments, stale memory corrections, table-priority fixes, and repeated intervention from Rork.

The final objective is not one successful property conversation.

The objective is to prove that IVX IA behaves consistently as a top-level Senior Software Engineer across the full production system.

==================================================
FINAL MISSION
==================================================

Complete IVX IA so the owner can use it as the permanent Senior Developer for IVX Holdings.

IVX IA must reliably:

1. Understand the owner.
2. Preserve context.
3. Inspect the live system.
4. Reason like a senior engineer.
5. Create real tasks.
6. Execute approved work.
7. Test changes.
8. Deploy safely.
9. Verify production.
10. Return evidence.

No narrative substitution.

No fake execution.

No lost context.

No repeated owner explanations.

==================================================
P0 — FREEZE AND VERIFY THE RECENT CONTEXT FIXES
==================================================

Verify the recently reported fixes are durable:

- stale ownerState overwrite repair;
- pending-action persistence;
- freshest-state reads before writes;
- buildWhereWeWereSummary correction;
- most-recent-action recall;
- property-table priority;
- direct Supabase routing;
- authorization follow-up routing;
- GitHub/Render SHA parity.

Run the exact acceptance conversation repeatedly.

Required conversation:

Owner:
“¿Cuántas propiedades tenemos?”

IVX IA:
Requests permission only if required.

Owner:
“La quiero ahora y yo te autorizo.”

IVX IA:
Returns the real property count from production.

Owner:
“¿Cuántas están activas?”

IVX IA:
Returns the real active count while preserving context.

Owner:
“Muéstrame las últimas cinco.”

IVX IA:
Returns the latest relevant records from the same data domain.

Owner:
“¿Dónde nos quedamos?”

IVX IA:
Correctly summarizes the active property investigation.

Run this sequence:

- 25 times in the same session;
- after app refresh;
- after app restart;
- after logout/login;
- after backend restart;
- after Render restart;
- after switching English to Spanish;
- after several unrelated questions;
- after long conversation history.

Required result:

100% pass.

One failure means the context layer is not complete.

==================================================
P0 — ELIMINATE ALL STALE-STATE BUGS
==================================================

Audit the full IVX IA state machine for the same defect pattern.

Search for:

- stale object snapshots;
- writes based on old state;
- overwriting fresh pending actions;
- non-atomic updates;
- race conditions;
- duplicate writes;
- out-of-order events;
- last-write-wins corruption;
- stale conversation memory;
- stale active task IDs;
- stale authorization state;
- stale tool results;
- stale deployment status;
- stale worker status.

Inspect all reads and writes related to:

- conversations;
- messages;
- owner state;
- pending actions;
- approvals;
- tasks;
- tools;
- jobs;
- deployments;
- memory;
- production state;
- evidence.

Use atomic database operations, transactions, version checks, or optimistic concurrency where appropriate.

Do not fix only the lines already identified.

Audit the complete pattern across the repository.

==================================================
P0 — AUTHORITATIVE INTENT ROUTING
==================================================

Create one authoritative routing layer.

Every owner request must be classified into one of these categories:

1. Information request
2. Explanation request
3. Architecture review
4. Code review
5. Bug diagnosis
6. Read-only data query
7. Data mutation
8. Code change
9. QA request
10. Deployment request
11. Rollback request
12. Task status
13. Approval response
14. Cancellation response
15. General conversation

Routing requirements:

Information request:
Read live data and answer.

Explanation request:
Answer directly with senior reasoning.

Read-only query:
Execute the authorized inspection and return evidence.

Code change:
Diagnose, explain, create a real task, execute after approval, test, deploy, verify.

Approval response:
Attach to the latest valid pending action.

Task status:
Read live task data.

Deployment request:
Verify commit, approval, deploy, health and parity.

General conversation:
Answer naturally without creating a worker task.

Never route a read-only data question to deployment.

Never route an approval reply to the LLM as a new question.

Never create a generic task when no task is required.

==================================================
P0 — TRUE SENIOR DEVELOPER REASONING
==================================================

IVX IA must not prove seniority by saying:

“I am a senior developer.”

It must prove seniority through its work.

For technical problems, IVX IA must:

- identify facts;
- separate facts from assumptions;
- inspect live evidence;
- identify probable root causes;
- compare solution options;
- explain tradeoffs;
- consider security;
- consider performance;
- consider scalability;
- consider maintainability;
- recommend the safest approach;
- estimate impact;
- create a real execution path;
- verify the outcome.

For simple questions, answer simply.

Do not produce an eight-step plan for a basic count query.

For complex questions, provide complete engineering reasoning.

==================================================
P0 — REAL EXECUTION, NOT NARRATIVE
==================================================

The following statements are prohibited unless backed by real execution:

- “I am executing now.”
- “I created the task.”
- “I deployed the change.”
- “The issue is fixed.”
- “Production is verified.”
- “Everything is under control.”

Every execution claim must include:

- task ID;
- worker ID;
- current state;
- files changed;
- commit SHA;
- test result;
- deployment ID;
- production SHA;
- health result;
- timestamp;
- trace ID.

Allowed task states:

PENDING_APPROVAL

QUEUED

RUNNING

TESTING

DEPLOYING

VERIFYING

COMPLETED

FAILED

BLOCKED

CANCELLED

No unsupported success language.

==================================================
P0 — FULL AUTONOMOUS ENGINEERING PIPELINE
==================================================

Every approved engineering request must follow:

Owner request

↓

Intent classification

↓

Live inspection

↓

Root-cause analysis

↓

Implementation plan

↓

Owner approval when required

↓

Real task creation

↓

Worker assignment

↓

Code change

↓

Typecheck

↓

Lint

↓

Unit tests

↓

Integration tests

↓

Regression tests

↓

Security checks

↓

Commit

↓

GitHub push

↓

CI

↓

Render deployment

↓

Production verification

↓

Evidence persistence

↓

Owner report

If any stage fails:

- stop unsafe progression;
- preserve state;
- report exact failure;
- expose logs;
- create recovery action;
- retry only when safe.

==================================================
P0 — LIVE PRODUCTION AWARENESS
==================================================

IVX IA must always know the current live state.

It must retrieve, not guess:

- GitHub HEAD;
- Render live SHA;
- production SHA;
- deployment ID;
- health status;
- boot time;
- API version;
- active workers;
- queued jobs;
- blocked jobs;
- pending approvals;
- open P0 issues;
- open P1 issues;
- recent test failures;
- recent deployments;
- current owner task.

Questions such as:

“What is live now?”

“What failed?”

“What is the highest priority?”

“What are the workers doing?”

“Why is this blocked?”

must return live answers.

If live data is unavailable, say exactly what failed.

==================================================
P1 — COMPLETE CONVERSATION MEMORY
==================================================

Persist conversation state in the backend.

Store:

- owner ID;
- conversation ID;
- active topic;
- active entity;
- pending action;
- pending approval;
- active task;
- active worker;
- latest tool result;
- latest deployment;
- unresolved question;
- previous decision;
- owner language;
- last verified production state.

Memory must work across:

- refresh;
- restart;
- logout/login;
- backend restart;
- Render restart;
- multiple devices;
- English;
- Spanish;
- mixed language;
- long conversations.

Test questions:

“Where were we?”

“What did you fix?”

“Continue.”

“Explain the last commit.”

“Show the last deployment.”

“What is still pending?”

All must return the correct live context.

==================================================
P1 — DEEP QA OF IVX IA
==================================================

Run at least 1,000 production-grade conversation and execution tests.

Required distribution:

- 200 natural conversation tests;
- 150 senior engineering reasoning tests;
- 150 read-only live-data queries;
- 150 multi-turn memory tests;
- 100 approval and authorization tests;
- 75 code execution tests;
- 50 deployment tests;
- 50 failure-recovery tests;
- 50 Spanish tests;
- 25 mixed-language tests.

Cover:

- React Native;
- Expo;
- TypeScript;
- Node;
- Hono;
- Supabase;
- PostgreSQL;
- AWS;
- Render;
- GitHub;
- CI/CD;
- authentication;
- authorization;
- database design;
- API design;
- performance;
- security;
- scaling;
- architecture;
- debugging;
- production incidents;
- app modules;
- owner controls;
- autonomous workers.

Targets:

- 100% correct approval attachment;
- 100% no fake execution claims;
- 100% no lost pending action;
- 100% no task-status hallucination;
- at least 99% correct intent routing;
- at least 99% correct follow-up context;
- 0 unnecessary clarification loops in known-context cases;
- 0 regression from restart or reconnect.

==================================================
P1 — FULL APP QA
==================================================

IVX IA must also inspect and understand the entire IVX platform.

Run QA across:

- Owner login;
- registration;
- password recovery;
- members;
- investors;
- buyers;
- properties;
- deals;
- reels;
- messages;
- media;
- documents;
- transactions;
- Admin Hub;
- Owner Dashboard;
- Autonomous Dashboard;
- variables;
- Supabase;
- Render;
- AWS;
- GitHub;
- CI/CD;
- notifications;
- uploads;
- realtime;
- offline recovery;
- session persistence;
- security;
- performance.

IVX IA must be able to explain the status of each module from live evidence.

==================================================
P1 — OWNER EXPERIENCE
==================================================

The owner must never need to ask Rork:

- what IVX IA is doing;
- what failed;
- what changed;
- where the chat went;
- whether a task was actually created;
- whether production was deployed;
- whether the result is real.

Inside IVX IA Chat, show:

- current task;
- current worker;
- status;
- progress;
- latest action;
- files changed;
- test result;
- deployment;
- evidence;
- blocker;
- next step.

Add a clear Live Work view connected to real task data.

==================================================
P1 — RESPONSE QUALITY
==================================================

IVX IA responses must be:

- direct;
- natural;
- technically accurate;
- concise for simple questions;
- detailed for complex engineering work;
- context-aware;
- evidence-driven;
- free of generic filler;
- free of false confidence;
- free of repeated clarification.

Do not expose raw internal tool names unless useful.

Explain capabilities in normal language first.

==================================================
FINAL OWNER ACCEPTANCE TEST
==================================================

Rork must perform a live owner demonstration.

The owner should be able to complete all of these in IVX IA Chat:

1. Ask a production-data question.
2. Authorize the read.
3. Receive the exact live answer.
4. Ask a follow-up.
5. Preserve context.
6. Report a real bug.
7. Receive root-cause analysis.
8. Approve a fix.
9. See a real task created.
10. Watch the worker execute.
11. Receive test results.
12. Receive commit SHA.
13. Receive deployment ID.
14. Verify production SHA.
15. Restart the app.
16. Ask “Where were we?”
17. Continue from the correct state.
18. Ask for current highest priority.
19. Receive the real task-based answer.
20. Ask for the latest evidence.

All 20 steps must pass in production.

==================================================
FINAL EVIDENCE PACKAGE
==================================================

Return one final evidence package containing:

- root causes fixed;
- files changed;
- migrations;
- tests executed;
- tests passed;
- tests failed;
- remaining failures;
- coverage;
- intent-routing results;
- memory results;
- approval results;
- execution results;
- Git commit SHA;
- GitHub HEAD;
- Render live SHA;
- production SHA;
- SHA parity;
- deployment ID;
- health result;
- worker status;
- task IDs;
- screenshots;
- recording of the 20-step owner acceptance test;
- APK version;
- APK SHA-256;
- Android physical-device result;
- iOS status clearly marked;
- unresolved DEVICE REQUIRED items.

==================================================
FINAL VERDICT RULE
==================================================

Do not call IVX IA “10/10” because one workflow works.

Do not call IVX IA “Senior Developer VERIFIED” because a report says PASS.

IVX IA may be declared 10/10 only when:

- context survives reliably;
- approvals attach correctly;
- live tools execute correctly;
- senior reasoning is consistent;
- autonomous tasks execute end to end;
- deployments are verified;
- all claims include evidence;
- the owner can see live work;
- restart recovery works;
- the complete 20-step owner acceptance test passes;
- no open P0 defects remain;
- all remaining limitations are explicitly documented.

Until then, continue fixing, testing, deploying and verifying.

EXECUTE THIS NOW.

Do not return another narrative-only response.

Complete the system, demonstrate it live, and return factual production evidence.
